Description: Tell one trusted client which window the person points at, and show it
 Adds zyantrik_window_locator_v1, a private protocol offered only to the one
 client labwc launches itself on a pre-connected socket from
 <yantrik locator="/absolute/program" private="app ids"> (launch-client.c),
 and again as soon as it exits (at most every 5 s). labwc starts it only when
 every rc.xml it read, and the program, are root's and writable by no one
 else (and the directories they are in), and the private list is set; the
 command and the list are taken once, when labwc starts.
 .
 The person's gesture is checked here: `at` is answered with a window only
 while a pointer button is held at the cursor (the drag), and `focused` only
 within 2 s after the new YantrikLocate action (Super+Y), once. A picture,
 rendered offscreen from that window's own scene subtree (scene-capture.c)
 into a sealed memory file, needs a fresh answer: only the window the most
 recent answer named, within 2 s, and once. Windows on the private list are
 named without a title and never pictured; windows on other workspaces are
 never named. Every picture is logged. At most 120 answers and 2 pictures a
 second; nothing while the session is locked. The point lookup looks through
 the client's own surfaces (its drag overlay) and stops at anyone else's.
 .
 Virtual pointer and keyboard can still synthesize both gestures: this holds
 the launched client to the person's action, and is not a boundary against
 programs running as the person (yantrikos/yantrik-os#414, #476).
 Built for Yantrik OS's Y Anywhere (design/y-anywhere-2026-11-22.md).
Author: Yantrik OS <dev@yantrikos.com>
Forwarded: not-yet
Last-Update: 2026-11-23
